{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.5,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Catch UnicodeDecodeError in _git (or the _committed_toml read) and re-raise it as ConfigError so undecodable git output keeps the documented exit-2 ConfigError path","criteria":["error-handling","edge-cases"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py:65: encoding=\"utf-8\",","src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py:69: except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as exc:","UnicodeDecodeError is a ValueError subclass, not an OSError or SubprocessError, so this except clause does not catch it","src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py:16-17: docstring says the gate 'fails closed with :class:`~rebar.config.ConfigError` ... so does any failure to read the committed file'","src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py:120-122: caller only handles `except config.ConfigError` -> prints 'verify-opcert: ...' and returns 2"],"finding":"With strict encoding=\"utf-8\", invalid UTF-8 in git output (e.g. a committed rebar.toml/pyproject.toml that isn't UTF-8, or non-UTF-8 stderr) raises UnicodeDecodeError from subprocess.run. _git does not catch it, so it escapes as a raw traceback instead of the ConfigError the module promises for any failure to read the committed file.","id":"0","impact":0.27,"location":"src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py:69","norm_id":"nbc8ae1697257a3e2","priority":0.27,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["origin/main carries a rebar.toml saved as cp1252/latin-1 (e.g. a non-ASCII comment): verify-opcert crashes with a UnicodeDecodeError traceback instead of exit 2 and a clear message","On Windows, this used to decode as cp1252 and reach tomllib, so the crash is new on Windows"],"suggeste